# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 2b (partner opens 1C).
title: Partner opens 1♣: a weak raise
id: L02-09
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3
student: S
board: 9
dealer: N
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A95    K97    Q52    AJ64
  E  K763   A654   K97    T7
  S  84     QT2    J83    K9532
  W  QJT2   J83    AT64   Q8

auction:
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 2C*    = 6-9 points and club support
     key: 6 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton spade is 7, and five clubs. Raise.
     not Pass: Did you count 7 points? With 6 or more, find a response.
     not 1NT: Did you check the list from the top? With five clubs, the raise comes first.
     not 3C: 3♣ shows an opening hand or better. Did you count 7?
     not *: With 6-9 points and club support, can you raise partner?
  W Pass
  N Pass   = A minimum: no game
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 1♣ promised four or more clubs, so your five give your side at
  least nine. Your 2♣ showed 6-9 points with support. With 14, partner can
  count no more than 23 for your side, and a club game needs about 28. She
  passes. North is declarer, because she bid clubs first, and so East will
  lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E S3  S S4  W SJ  N SA
  2   N CA  E C7  S C2  W C8
      note: Declarer draws trumps.
  3   N C4  E CT  S CK  W CQ
      note: Trumps are all drawn.
  4   S H2  W H3  N HK  E HA
      note: Lead a heart to set up a trick there.
  5   E S6  S S8  W ST  N S9
  6   W SQ  N S5  E S7  S C3
      note: Dummy ruffs the third spade.
  7   S HQ  W H8  N H7  E H4
      note: Keep leading hearts.
  8   S HT  W HJ  N H9  E H5
      note: Hearts again.
  9   W S2  N C6  E SK  S D3
      note: Declarer ruffs again.
  10  N D2  E D7  S DJ  W DA
      note: Now diamonds, to set up a trick there.
  11  W D4  N DQ  E DK  S D8
  12  E D9  S C9  W D6  N D5
  13  S C5  W DT  N CJ  E H6
      note: 8 tricks: 2♣ made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then use the long clubs to ruff.

  2♣ made exactly. Your raise showed the fit and your strength in one bid,
  and partner knew to stop.
